<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haffon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Huffon, Hufon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haffon, also written Huffon, was the last independent king of Whydah, or Hueda, on the coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, reigning from 1708. His kingdom prospered from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> through its port, where several European companies kept forts. In 1727 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agaja">King Agaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> invaded and destroyed his capital, Savi, and Haffon fled westwards; his attempts to recover his kingdom with the help of exiles and allies failed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haffon.jpg" alt="Haffon" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rama · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Personnages_de_la_C%C3%B4te_des_Graines_mg_8481.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
